    <name>
      <text>29.1 Vector equations</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>a) i) Find rational constants \(a\) and \(b\), such that \(a{@matrix1@} + b{@matrix2@} = {@matrixAns@}\).</p>
<p align="right">\(a =\) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</p>
<p align="right">\(b =\) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]]</p>
<p align="right"><b>(2)</b></p>
<p>[[feedback:prt1]]</p>
<p><br>b) i) Find whole numbers \(x\), \(y\) and \(z\) such that \(x{@matrix1@} + y{@matrix2@} = z{@matrixAns@}\).</p>
<p align="right">\(x =\) [[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]]</p>
<p align="right">\(y =\) [[input:ans4]] [[validation:ans4]]</p>
<p align="right">\(z =\) [[input:ans5]] [[validation:ans5]]</p>
<p align="right"><b>(1)</b></p>
<p>[[feedback:prt2]]</p>
<p>b) ii) Calculate the magnitudes of the three vectors for your chosen whole number values of  \(x\), \(y\) and \(z\).<br><i>Write your answers fully simplified in the form \(n\sqrt{m}\) for integers \(n,m\) by writing \(n*sqrt(m)\).</i></p>
<p align="right">\(\left| x{@matrix1@} \right| =\) [[input:ans6]] [[validation:ans6]]</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt3]]</p>
<p align="right">\(\left| y{@matrix2@} \right| =\) [[input:ans7]] [[validation:ans7]]</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt4]]</p>
<p align="right">\(\left| z{@matrixAns@} \right| =\) [[input:ans8]] [[validation:ans8]]</p>
<p>[[feedback:prt5]]</p>
<p align="right"><b>(6)</b></p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
